<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dakhla</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Villa Cisneros</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dakhla is a city on a long peninsula on the Atlantic coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-sahara">Western Sahara</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> founded it in 1884 as Villa Cisneros, a trading post and fort, and it became the capital of the colony of Río de Oro. After the Spanish withdrawal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritania">Mauritania</a> held it from 1976 until 1979, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> took over the area; it is now a fishing port and the main town of the south of the territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dakhla.jpg" alt="Dakhla" width="320" height="140" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: YoTuT from United States · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dakhla,_Western_Sahara_(11).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
